#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115072 :question/id #uuid "239ee94c-c3d9-5955-8cdd-afff77ec3279" :question/math-academy-id "e-4716" :question/problem "Is \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$ \nan elementary matrix?" :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation.\n\nThe given matrix $E$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I_2$ by applying the elementary row operation $R_2:= R_2+(-5) R_1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115073 :question/id #uuid "40cdd39f-29c3-5dad-9708-02c3e0de6acb" :question/math-academy-id "e-4718" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$$\nE = \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\displaystyle \\frac{2}{5}}\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $E$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{2}{5} & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n$$\nE^{-1} =\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\displaystyle \\frac{5}{2}}\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115074 :question/id #uuid "ed71f469-f0e9-5016-846d-cb70d59ab3ea" :question/math-academy-id "e-4719" :question/problem "Find the product $E_1 E_{2}^{-1},$ where $E_1 =\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}1 & 0 \\\\ - 5 & 1\\end{array} \\right]}$ and $E_2 =\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}1 & - 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{array} \\right]}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $E_1$ and $E_2$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find $E_2^{-1}.$ We write down $E_2$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\nE_2^{-1} =\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product $E_1 E_{2}^{-1}\\mathbin{:}$\n$$\nE_1 E_{2}^{-1} =\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}1 & 0 \\\\ - 5 & 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n= \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}1 & 2 \\\\ - 5 & - 9\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115735 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bfc713a-679b-5cfa-9d6f-08a36b86fb51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436496} {:answer/id #uuid "a74234e5-d97b-566c-bed3-339abfaef5b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ -11 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436498} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f73949-1a41-5465-a743-a686174de006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436499} {:answer/id #uuid "c0bb3be0-28be-55c7-a77b-ae02e4febeba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436506} {:answer/id #uuid "e25a7759-8c03-50b5-a54a-8024f5ffd9a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bfc713a-679b-5cfa-9d6f-08a36b86fb51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436496} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed86b220-5180-5369-9230-c6b72b1d1579" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1814a01e-7b9b-5bac-ab6c-86bbec04e6cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-31932" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{E}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{2}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{2}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{2}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c89d58a-c775-5607-8754-ada001af1092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113395} {:answer/id #uuid "3cd6d02f-02aa-5e2c-bc02-c7d907a619af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113396} {:answer/id #uuid "68af6deb-1ead-5d87-9d0e-40a52ee56971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113397} {:answer/id #uuid "75472ff7-0158-5d87-bff6-8f21d2b88261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113398} {:answer/id #uuid "7abf9602-3611-5266-a907-f46b7e931769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113399}] :answer-field/id #uuid "38b84383-009a-51c9-ab00-502af2b98f44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113394}] :question/id #uuid "24f9b684-ed46-5b7d-84d3-2382910d4817" :question/math-academy-id "q-31963" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115839 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a081c073-7785-5822-a590-7bfe5b3a0d78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459993} {:answer/id #uuid "b0a6c82a-ea16-5ff3-8bdf-84c0339a862e" :a