value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459997} :answer-field/id #uuid "12022d23-fdca-5fdc-a369-46e825b1e2e8" :answer-field/key "$S=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460865} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "807a46a6-8dfc-5144-9fec-499af330205e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668078} {:answer/id #uuid "82d9ff93-8e2c-5a8a-8790-649277a064f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "807a46a6-8dfc-5144-9fec-499af330205e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668078} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3d8a7c7-5aac-54c6-b7df-185eefd0a6aa" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "60c27a10-b6b0-5a54-9d51-0c91bf9fbc6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42591" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $P$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =P\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrices $Q$ and $S$ are not elementary matrices because they can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ is an elementary matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115840 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa76d599-e312-5edc-88d9-382bbf1fad4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113978} {:answer/id #uuid "ae2461e8-8778-528d-a295-5694d36bf193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113979} {:answer/id #uuid "2e5d784b-1610-5078-b2e6-78e49eb36316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113980} {:answer/id #uuid "5fcab5d0-7297-5665-be04-530378c3a1ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113981} {:answer/id #uuid "70c38f86-b11a-5f10-8cde-87d0759a35db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113982}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7a3d25a7-6de6-5674-be48-59a5c70032d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113977}] :question/id #uuid "71715852-342c-5903-aaea-2bbb1035b850" :question/math-academy-id "q-42601" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle E = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115841 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d5cf453-a524-596c-a71c-3cc10ff9251a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550509} {:answer/id #uuid "9f574a63-4cd5-5ba3-aee2-b3411a92aab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550776} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f3902b-ad8b-5c0c-8a37-a910843374dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550785} {:answer/id #uuid "cb2def03-42ec-5d22-9a67-872732233e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550915} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d061de-733c-5ff8-b08f-66b5ba33a70c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f574a63-4cd5-5ba3-aee2-b3411a92aab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550776} :answer-field/id #uuid "4eb2360f-9c37-5242-a36d-bf3f7078ccc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113983}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e24eefb5-7086-59e4-b488-5ab843ea61ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-42696" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{E}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{1}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{1}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{1}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & -7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+7{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115842 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34da3084-a21c-5f11-a32e-01588ddf5fab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436483} {:answer/id #uuid "bba143df-3184-57ce-bc93-47ed7a3522c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436503} {:answer/id #uuid "bcd5f231-30de-5f93-92ba-901fd84afa6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436505} {:answer/id #uuid "c7c585a9-2f07-5403-bcb1-dabce9f67e3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436508} {:answer/id #uuid "e5167b06-7c0b-5f26-8c68-4d6d734b259b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcd5f231-30de-5f93-92ba-901fd84afa6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436505} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3e2b631-2958-5e53-a350-a255155a7da2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a0ff6849-42fb-5905-961f-eb146b05e241" :question/math-academy-id "q-42697" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265973 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82c68fda-0f42-5c48-9715-68ca5d6ebb8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463898} {:answer/id #uuid "ae743fce-b45e-5abc-bd86-752ba9bcbc46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae743fce-b45e-5abc-bd86-752ba9bcbc46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463899} :answer-field/id #uuid "01448568-f01a-5eb2-9776-853e263f1da6" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464883} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78b1bf75-980f-5157-a21e-c5aaa7d1d2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463900} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2a98f4-65b2-5c86-bfcb-8b40e5c7595b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce2a98f4-65b2-5c86-bfcb-8b40e5c7595b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463901} :answer-field/id #uuid "124e1032-53d8-59c4-9767-8aa9b08c5f27" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11393e6b-38fe-5ee8-a898-8839130cc2bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463902} {:answer/id #uuid "1d89d028-e268-579c-869b-ea7d5ab042e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11393e6b-38fe-5ee8-a898-8839130cc2bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463902} :answer-field/id #uuid "2539df0a-7237-5aec-a2e8-de82405d21b5" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6ec5e472-dc1d-5891-bb93-866a6d9b3914" :question/math-academy-id "q-130774" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are elementary matrices."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265975 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26738c1b-cd2a-54b0-a9a2-e6873308bbee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263334} {:answer/id #uuid "40e0c5ba-412c-5d2d-a4d7-9da37d589299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263574} {:answer/id #uuid "85b8f931-2c64-551b-b836-fdf84643e914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264153} {:answer/id #uuid "c34841c6-9ef8-5a10-adaa-f5c0401a208a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264703} {:answer/id #uuid "e473ae6b-cf31-5bc4-acef-f7158942ad3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c34841c6-9ef8-5a10-adaa-f5c0401a208a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264703} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2e7ebfa-6118-5fc8-b043-a2c4fd2d2256" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4923d93e-8e1d-5354-994f-77bd317d2271" :question/math-academy-id "q-130781" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $B$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+10{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 10 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{B}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1892f5f0-6368-5dfc-9db2-22b92c17610e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263234} {:answer/id #uuid "b00d293f-c42e-500d-8daa-fbaf78bc3619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264519} {:answer/id #uuid "dceacc3f-3a8c-55ea-a4b3-ef3fc223628b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 24 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264925} {:answer/id #uuid "ea897ab9-67ce-5b28-a039-56ca3165c521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265042} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2c9353-6755-575d-a0e0-7a0bf2c5bf04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 24 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b00d293f-c42e-500d-8daa-fbaf78bc3619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264519} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1f54dd4-2096-5ae8-b637-43e81f2f6482" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "51436b19-ea29-5947-96ab-9dd34a7a3995" :question/math-academy-id "q-130812" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{E}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{2}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{2}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{2}:=(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{2}^{-1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0449b553-1b65-5cac-8598-b0d8a270a950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263039} {:answer/id #uuid "08cf208e-4a67-56fb-af8e-a3fd93304b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263084} {:answer/id #uuid "79e21f99-e8cc-51c3-a318-a7ddd869b864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264057} {:answer/id #uuid "7e60b2a6-6056-5ea2-8a17-c6be4b8de34e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}19 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264091} {:answer/id #uuid "9e4de5ce-9af6-520d-b7aa-ae9f2db45567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 & -7 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0449b553-1b65-5cac-8598-b0d8a270a950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263039} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcf3b9f2-af48-548d-9af3-5530034cb7ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d8b759c1-7acc-5a06-82c3-b179ddb571b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-130823" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{E}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{2}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{2}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{2}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}21 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299786 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92a6fafe-efb0-5881-a