x into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{1}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-8){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}49 & -8 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393334 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd8e97f8-62db-59df-a835-2809adb5e257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393336} {:answer/id #uuid "e1f3711d-8e3f-5c0d-a6bb-bbd6d27addc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393337} {:answer/id #uuid "164bdc4b-a7d3-5f5f-a7c5-a7306117cef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393338} {:answer/id #uuid "e56e83a6-e9d3-5d94-bcd2-7fba1ec33e6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393339} {:answer/id #uuid "09fe462f-59ae-5f04-b0f3-8af36fa3770f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd8e97f8-62db-59df-a835-2809adb5e257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393336} :answer-field/id #uuid "3854ffe7-363e-5eb6-88e6-d70a996900b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bd74f139-452a-58af-a7f9-3d3621835dfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-73647" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{E}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{2}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{2}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{2}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393341 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7deb948-54b4-534d-b47c-0134061b79e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393343} {:answer/id #uuid "5602e756-3d3f-58a5-a71c-b94b98cc37d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answ